  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you have implemented a disaster recovery strategy for a data analytics application with a multi-regional architecture. To validate the effectiveness of the disaster recovery plan, you must perform periodic tests. Which of the following options is the best approach for testing the disaster recovery plan while minimizing the impact on production workloads and ensuring accurate test results?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Perform a chaos engineering test by introducing random failures into the production environment.<br/>B. Use a scheduled maintenance window to perform disaster recovery tests on the production environment.<br/>C. Create a separate environment that mirrors the production environment and use real-time database replication to conduct disaster recovery tests.<br/>D. Create a temporary environment using a recent database snapshot and simulate a disaster recovery scenario.",
